---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ProjectInvitation from '../components/ProjectInvitation.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Services"><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Services</span><h1>Software that moves<br/>your business forward.</h1><p class="lead">From a first release to a connected business platform, I help define what needs to be built—and take responsibility for delivering it.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container grid"><article class="card"><span class="number">01 / IDEA TO LAUNCH</span><h2>Launch a new product</h2><p>Turn your idea into a working first release. Start with the essential journeys and build the systems that support them.</p><ul class="list"><li>Requirements and launch scope</li><li>Customer apps or web product</li><li>Backend and administration tools</li><li>Testing, deployment, and handover</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/contact">Discuss your first release →</a></article><article class="card"><span class="number">02 / CONNECTED OPERATIONS</span><h2>Build your business platform</h2><p>Connect customers, service providers, and your team with software built around how your business actually works.</p><ul class="list"><li>Customer and provider applications</li><li>Staff dashboards and workflows</li><li>APIs, data, and integrations</li><li>Backend and cloud deployment</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/contact">Discuss your platform →</a></article><article class="card"><span class="number">03 / THE NEXT CHAPTER</span><h2>Improve an existing product</h2><p>Extend your software as your needs evolve. Mobile development remains available as a focused engagement.</p><ul class="list"><li>Flutter and native Android development</li><li>New features and integrations</li><li>Architecture and backend improvements</li><li>Maintenance and release support</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/contact">Discuss your existing product →</a></article></div></section><section class="section dark"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">For complex builds</span><h2>Get clarity<br/>before committing.</h2><p class="lead">A paid discovery and planning phase gives us a concrete starting point for a larger project.</p></div><div><h3>Your discovery deliverables</h3><p class="muted">Agreed business workflows, first-release scope, reviewable milestones, technical dependencies, and an estimate. The discovery scope and fee are agreed before work begins.</p><a class="button" href="/contact">Discuss discovery ↗</a></div></div></section><ProjectInvitation /></SiteLayout><style>.card h2{font-size:1.9rem}.card{display:flex;flex-direction:column}.card .text-link{margin-top:auto;align-self:flex-start}</style>
